WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.869
"Nail," said Dad . Joy reached into her

2
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:12.023
sack. "Nail!" she said, handing him

3
00:00:12.024 --> 00:00:15.973
one. Dad pounded it into a board with his

4
00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:18.938
hammer. "Good job!" said

5
00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:22.804
Joy. Joy and her dad had been busy all

6
00:00:22.805 --> 00:00:27.414
morning. They had moved Grandpa's wood up to the elm

7
00:00:27.415 --> 00:00:32.109
trees. Then they bought more wooden boards and posts at the

8
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:37.525
lumberyard. Dad put two posts in the ground and built a frame for the tree house

9
00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:42.034
floor. When he was finished, he looked at Joy with a

10
00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:46.126
frown. "Partner," he said, "we have a

11
00:00:46.127 --> 00:00:50.106
problem." "What's wrong?" asked Joy with

12
00:00:50.107 --> 00:00:56.378
surprise. "See this wood we bought for the floor?" said Dad, pointing at a pile of 12

13
00:00:56.379 --> 00:00:59.058
boards. "They are two and a half meters

14
00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:04.036
long." Joy looked at the boards and then looked up at the frame Dad had

15
00:01:04.037 --> 00:01:07.874
built. She tilted her head and narrowed her

16
00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:09.657
eyes. Then she

17
00:01:09.658 --> 00:01:12.835
smiled. "Those boards look too

18
00:01:12.836 --> 00:01:16.616
long." "You've got a good set of eyes!" said

19
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:22.308
Dad. "The frame is two meters long, so we need to shorten each board by half a

20
00:01:22.309 --> 00:01:26.195
meter." Dad and Joy knelt by one

21
00:01:26.196 --> 00:01:31.477
board. "Hold this tape measure at the end of the board," Dad said, handing her the

22
00:01:31.478 --> 00:01:34.589
measure. Then he pulled the tape along the

23
00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.395
edge. "That's 25 centimeters," said

24
00:01:38.396 --> 00:01:40.592
Joy. Dad pulled the tape some

25
00:01:40.593 --> 00:01:43.933
more. "And that's

26
00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:49.052
50!" "Now I mark it with a pencil," explained Dad as he drew a black

27
00:01:49.053 --> 00:01:51.541
line. "That's where we will cut the

28
00:01:51.542 --> 00:01:55.660
board." "Should we measure and mark all of them?" asked

29
00:01:55.661 --> 00:01:57.641
Joy. "Yes," said

30
00:01:57.642 --> 00:02:00.803
Dad. "Then I'll cut them down to the right

31
00:02:00.804 --> 00:02:01.955
size. And you know

32
00:02:01.956 --> 00:02:05.727
what? We can take the leftover wood to the recycling

33
00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:09.371
center." "Somebody else will be able to use it," said Joy.

34
00:02:09.372 --> 00:02:12.542
"Just like we used Grandpa's wood."

35
00:02:12.543 --> 00:02:18.489
By late afternoon Dad had finished nailing the tree house floor to the frame.

36
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:24.397
He and Joy sat on the back end of the truck and looked up at their work.

37
00:02:24.398 --> 00:02:27.363
"What's next?" asked Joy.

38
00:02:27.364 --> 00:02:29.442
"Let's recycle that extra wood.

39
00:02:29.443 --> 00:02:33.543
We might find a few things we need too," said Dad.

40
00:02:33.544 --> 00:02:38.179
They got in the truck and drove down the hill to the road.

41
00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:42.532
When they reached the center, Joy hopped out of the truck.

42
00:02:42.533 --> 00:02:48.430
She liked looking up at the mountains of crushed cardboard and smashed soda cans.

43
00:02:48.431 --> 00:02:52.204
She saw Mr. Ramirez, Carlos' father.

44
00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:59.158
He was in charge of sorting all the metal—brass, tin, iron, steel, and copper.

45
00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:02.759
"Hello, Mr. Ramirez," called Joy.

46
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.187
"Dad and I are building a tree house!

47
00:03:05.188 --> 00:03:07.870
Do you have anything we can use?"

48
00:03:07.871 --> 00:03:11.416
"Well, let's see," said Mr. Ramirez.

49
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:13.281
"Do you need a bucket?"

50
00:03:13.282 --> 00:03:17.758
"We might," replied Joy. "Thanks!"

51
00:03:17.759 --> 00:03:20.554
Dad was looking in a cardboard box.

52
00:03:20.555 --> 00:03:23.824
"Here are some old hooks," he said.

53
00:03:23.825 --> 00:03:28.396
"The kids can hang stuff on those," said Mr. Ramirez.

54
00:03:28.397 --> 00:03:32.053
Joy dropped the hooks into her bucket.

55
00:03:32.054 --> 00:03:36.291
"What's this?" asked Joy. "A wheel?"

56
00:03:36.292 --> 00:03:40.607
"It's a special kind of wheel," said Mr. Ramirez.

57
00:03:40.608 --> 00:03:42.309
"It's called a pulley.

58
00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.619
You use it with a rope to help lift something."

59
00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.590
Joy turned to her dad.

60
00:03:47.591 --> 00:03:49.676
"Do we need one?"

61
00:03:49.677 --> 00:03:54.635
"Take it," he said. "We can use it."

62
00:03:54.636 --> 00:03:57.810
"Let's take this pole too," said Joy.

63
00:03:57.811 --> 00:04:00.360
"It might be good for something."

64
00:04:00.361 --> 00:04:04.831
Then Dad found some sheets of tin leaning against a wall.

65
00:04:04.832 --> 00:04:09.039
"Our tree house roof!" cried Joy.

66
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.664
And that wasn't all.

67
00:04:10.665 --> 00:04:15.291
They also found a small window frame and an old door.

68
00:04:15.292 --> 00:04:21.646
They piled everything in the back of the truck and drove home.

